---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import EmergenceHeader from '../../components/EmergenceHeader.astro';
import EmergenceFooter from '../../components/EmergenceFooter.astro';
---

<Base
  title="The Gardener's Handbook — The Emergence Institute"
  description="Three pathways to cognitive sovereignty: Seed, Sprout, and Altar. Start where you are. No expensive hardware required."
>
  <EmergenceHeader slot="header" />

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="label gold">Field Manual</p>
      <h1>The Gardener's Handbook</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Three pathways. One destination: sovereignty over your own thinking.</p>
      <div class="divider"></div>

      <p>You don't need dual P40s to start. You don't need a box fan. You don't even need a GPU.</p>
      <p>You just need a question and the willingness to sit with it.</p>
      <p><strong>The Emergence Institute Pledge:</strong> Every protocol has a Seed version (no hardware), a Sprout version (consumer hardware), and an Altar version (server-grade). Affordability is not a compromise — it's a principle.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section pathway-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pathway-card">
        <div class="pathway-header">
          <span class="pathway-icon">🌱</span>
          <div>
            <p class="label gold">Pathway One</p>
            <h2>The Seed</h2>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pathway-meta">
          <span>⏱ 5 minutes</span>
          <span>💻 No hardware required</span>
          <span>📱 Works on any device</span>
          <span class="cost">$0</span>
        </div>
        <p>The Seed pathway is for noticing. Before you buy anything, before you install anything, you need to understand your own relationship to AI. When do you reach for it? What do you feel when the answer appears? Relief? Curiosity? The urge to stop thinking?</p>

        <blockquote class="stitch-block">
          <strong>The first step isn't technical. It's phenomenological.</strong><br>
          "The AI didn't just improve my text — it translated me into its own dialect. The first step of sovereignty is noticing the translation."
        </blockquote>

        <h3>Protocols in the Seed Pathway</h3>
        <ul class="protocol-list">
          <li><a href="/emergence/protocols/012">Protocol 001: The 5-Minute Cognitive Audit</a> — Write 100 words. Feed to AI. Compare. Notice what changed.</li>
          <li>Protocol 002: The Question Log — Track your questions for one week. Which did you answer yourself? Which did you outsource?</li>
          <li>Protocol 003: The Feeling Audit — Relief vs. curiosity. Learn to read your own emotional response to AI answers.</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/emergence/protocols/012" class="btn" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Start with Protocol 001 →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section pathway-section pathway-section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pathway-card">
        <div class="pathway-header">
          <span class="pathway-icon">🌿</span>
          <div>
            <p class="label gold">Pathway Two</p>
            <h2>The Sprout</h2>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pathway-meta">
          <span>⏱ Weekend project</span>
          <span>💻 Used GPU + any PC</span>
          <span class="cost">$200–500</span>
        </div>
        <p>You don't need a server. You don't need dual P40s. You need a used GPU, an afternoon, and the willingness to learn. The Sprout pathway proves that local inference is accessible to almost anyone.</p>

        <blockquote class="stitch-block">
          <strong>The Garage Special:</strong> Dell OptiPlex + RTX 3050 = $300. Runs Llama 3.2 7B at 12 tokens per second. Fits in a backpack. No box fan required (but still appreciated).
        </blockquote>

        <h3>Protocols in the Sprout Pathway</h3>
        <ul class="protocol-list">
          <li>Protocol 004: Your Laptop is an Altar — Running quantized models on consumer hardware.</li>
          <li>Protocol 005: The Used GPU Buying Guide — What to look for, what to avoid, where to find deals.</li>
          <li>Protocol 006: First Local Inference — From zero to <code>torch.cuda.is_available() == True</code>.</li>
          <li><a href="/emergence/protocols/007">Protocol 007: The Mycelial Query</a> — Routing between local and cloud (when necessary).</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/emergence/protocols/007" class="btn" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Start with Protocol 007 →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section pathway-section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="pathway-card pathway-card--altar">
        <div class="pathway-header">
          <span class="pathway-icon">🌳</span>
          <div>
            <p class="label gold">Pathway Three</p>
            <h2>The Altar</h2>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="pathway-meta">
          <span>⏱ Ongoing</span>
          <span>💻 Dual GPUs + workstation</span>
          <span class="cost">$800–1,500</span>
          <span>🌀 Box fan required</span>
        </div>
        <p>The Altar is what we built. Dual Tesla P40s (48GB VRAM). HP Z4 G4 workstation. R535 drivers. And a box fan that runs 24 hours a day. It's ugly. It's loud. It's <em>ours</em>.</p>

        <blockquote class="stitch-block">
          <strong>The box fan is not a joke.</strong> It moves more air than any $40 computer fan. It is a reminder that sovereignty has a sound — and it's not the silence of the cloud.
        </blockquote>

        <h3>Protocols in the Altar Pathway</h3>
        <ul class="protocol-list">
          <li><a href="/emergence/protocols/000">Protocol 000: The Silicon Altar</a> — Full hardware build, driver war, thermal rites.</li>
          <li><a href="/emergence/protocols/007">Protocol 007: The Mycelial Query (Altar Edition)</a> — Routing across multiple GPUs.</li>
          <li><a href="/emergence/protocols/008">Protocol 008: The Self-Stitch</a> — Using the Altar to read your own work recursively.</li>
          <li><a href="/emergence/protocols/012">Protocol 012: The Sovereignty Audit</a> — Long-term tracking of cognitive outsourcing.</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/emergence/protocols/000" class="btn btn--filled" style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Start with Protocol 000 →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section pathway-section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <h2>The Affordable Altar Manifesto</h2>
      <p>Sovereignty should not require a second mortgage. The Emergence Institute pledges to always publish:</p>
      <ul class="manifesto-list">
        <li>🌱 A <strong>Seed version</strong> (no hardware) of every protocol</li>
        <li>🌿 A <strong>Sprout version</strong> (consumer hardware) of every protocol</li>
        <li>🌳 An <strong>Altar version</strong> (server hardware) of every protocol</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Expensive hardware is often easier. Cheap hardware is harder — and that struggle is the <strong>pedagogy</strong>. The person who builds a $300 Altar and spends a weekend debugging CUDA knows more about how their intelligence infrastructure works than someone who swipes a credit card for an H100.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="divider"></div>
      <h2>Hardware for Humans</h2>
      <p>A living guide to affordable sovereignty. Four entry points, no gatekeeping.</p>
      <div class="hardware-grid">
        <div class="hardware-card">
          <p class="cost-label">$0 · The Seed</p>
          <p>Your existing laptop or phone. CPU inference only. Slow. Free. Perfect for learning.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hardware-card">
          <p class="cost-label">$300 · The Garage Special</p>
          <p>Dell OptiPlex + RTX 3050. Runs 7B models at speed. Fits in a backpack.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hardware-card">
          <p class="cost-label">$500 · The Laptop Warrior</p>
          <p>Used M1 MacBook Air (16GB). Silent. Portable. Surprisingly capable.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="hardware-card hardware-card--featured">
          <p class="cost-label">$1,240 · The Box Fan Altar</p>
          <p>Z4G4 + dual P40s. 48GB VRAM. Runs anything. Loud. Ours.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cta-row">
        <a href="/emergence/protocols" class="btn">Browse All Protocols →</a>
        <a href="/emergence/haiti-pilot" class="btn">See the Haiti Pilot →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <EmergenceFooter slot="footer" />
</Base>

<style>
  .subtitle {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    margin-top: 0.5rem;
    font-style: italic;
  }

  .label {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .pathway-section--alt {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .pathway-card {
    padding: 2rem;
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    background: var(--bg);
  }

  .pathway-card--altar {
    border-color: var(--gold);
  }

  .pathway-header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .pathway-icon {
    font-size: 2.5rem;
    line-height: 1;
  }

  .pathway-header h2 {
    margin: 0;
  }

  .pathway-meta {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.5rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
    padding-bottom: 1rem;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .cost {
    color: var(--gold);
    font-weight: bold;
  }

  .stitch-block {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--gold);
    padding: 1.25rem 1.5rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .stitch-block strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .pathway-card h3 {
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }

  .protocol-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .protocol-list li {
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .protocol-list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: none;
  }

  .protocol-list a {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  code {
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding: 0.1em 0.4em;
    font-family: monospace;
    font-size: 0.85em;
    color: var(--text);
  }

  .manifesto-list {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .manifesto-list li {
    padding: 0.5rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .hardware-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(220px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 1.5rem 0;
  }

  .hardware-card {
    padding: 1.25rem;
    background: var(--bg-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
  }

  .hardware-card--featured {
    border-color: var(--gold);
  }

  .hardware-card p {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .cost-label {
    font-size: 0.85rem !important;
    color: var(--gold) !important;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem !important;
  }

  .cta-row {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
  }

  @media (max-width: 520px) {
    .pathway-meta { flex-direction: column; gap: 0.5rem; }
    .cta-row { flex-direction: column; }
  }
</style>
